00:08:16.175 --> 00:08:17.935
inside PyTorch or Jax.

00:08:17.935 --> 00:08:18.055
leaks.

00:08:18.575 --> 00:08:23.255
Each extra software layer between the model description and the silicon burns cycles that

00:08:23.255 --> 00:08:24.415
could have been matrix math.

00:08:24.975 --> 00:08:29.375
And when thousands of chips pass partial results around, those layers stack up.

00:08:29.975 --> 00:08:35.075
Code written once for the exact interconnect and memory layout of a GB300 cluster strips

00:08:35.075 --> 00:08:37.015
that overhead where the waste is largest.

00:08:37.755 --> 00:08:43.735
Tesla made a similar call in 2019, leaving Nvidia's off-the-shelf self-driving computer for

00:08:43.735 --> 00:08:45.175
